      "text": "Logged recommendation data is not a random sample. Items appear in a log because a\nproduction policy chose to show them, so the training distribution is the policy's, not\nthe world's. IPS reweights each observation by the inverse of its propensity — the\nprobability that item was shown — to recover an unbiased estimate:\n\n    weighted_loss = sum_i ( loss_i / propensity_i )\n\nSeparately, and often more usefully, some datasets ship a *randomised exposure* log:\nimpressions generated by showing users uniformly random items. That log is unbiased by\nconstruction and needs no propensity model at all."
